X:69
T:Drunk at Night. BF11.69
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:3/4=40
S:MS11,c1800?.,Browne Coll.,Lakes
R:Air
O:England
A:North-West - Lake District
N:Exactly as written. Beware suspect note lengths and repeats.
N:Does not work at all well on fiddle, but very convincing when
N:midi set to Orchestral Harp.
N:This tune occupies three & 1/2 pages in MS.
N:Notes marked with a plus
N:sign have no stems in MS..The notes in the third strain that I have
N:marked as triplets are not marked so in MS..CGP
Z:vmp.Chris Partington
B:Village Music project, Browne 11
